/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   the chapter board — one engine, two hosts

   This is everything the chapter board is: the projection, the feed,
   the counting, the map and the panels under it. It was the body of
   /invoice/data/index.html until the console grew a Chapters view, at
   which point there were two places to fix a miscount instead of one.

   So it mounts rather than runs. `Chapters.markup(prefix)` returns the
   panels with every id carrying that prefix, and `Chapters.mount(opts)`
   binds them and starts polling. Nothing here owns a gate, a topbar, a
   status light or a footer — the host does, and is handed what it needs
   through onLive / onSource / onCount / onBanner. That is what lets the
   standalone page keep its own page chrome while the console's view sits
   inside a rail it knows nothing about.

   The prefix is not decoration. The console already has a `#tbody`, a
   `#live-txt` and a `#foot-count` of its own, and a second set under the
   same names would have the two boards quietly writing into each other.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
